# The base problems of the family repeated_reduction_mixin_builtin_binary: the check
# C.Equal(A.Plus(B)) of MIXINv2's Builtin BinNatPlus and BinNatEquality
# (the files of Builtin/ beside this file), A, B and C built as nested objects as
# MIXINv2/packages/mixinv2-library/tests/BinNatArithmeticTest.mixin.yaml builds
# them, the program shaped as ThreePlusFour.lambdalattice, read at church.
# The sums are those of problems/reduction_mixin_binary, the same programs in
# the fixed-width mixin encoding, and one pair each at 64 and 128 bits. A sum
# that fails has the result plus the power of two just above it, a new highest
# bit, so that the comparison must reach the top.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT of each is the Boolean of the equation, computed with integers.
# PROOF: plus descends on the receiver's halves and equality on both numerals'
# halves, every recursion on a finite numeral, and each class has one
# implementation of each member read; MIXINv2's evaluator reads the same YAML
# to the same Booleans at the three smaller sizes.
#
#   binary_point(?Point, ?Left, ?Right, ?Result)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
